      "description": "Inscription reads:\nSTANDING ROCK\nINYAN WOSLATA\nA famous sacred stone which many years ago came into possession of the Sioux. According to Dakota legend, it is a body of a young Indian woman with her child on her back who were [sic] left in camp she refused to accompany the tribe as they moved south. When others were sent back to find her, she was found to have turned to stone. The stone is held in reverence by the Sioux and it is placed here overlooking the waters and the empire once held by the mighty Sioux Nation.\nSponsored By\nLocal Lions Club\nAmerican Legion\n\nTribal Council 1963",
